WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:05.071
-Today, Senate Democrats cleared
a major procedural hurdle

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.740
on their way
to passing their urgent

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.674
and desperately needed
Covid relief bill

00:00:08.674 --> 00:00:11.777
with a tie breaking vote from
Vice President Kamala Harris.

00:00:11.777 --> 00:00:13.646
But the victory comes
after moderate senators

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:17.150
demanded the Democrats limit the
eligibility for direct payments.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.452
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:24.890
Donald Trump was bad
at pretty much everything

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:26.125
when it came to politics.

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:28.594
He lost the popular vote twice,
lost the House

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.563
in 2018,
in the Senate this year,

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:32.532
got impeached twice
and never cracked

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:34.300
50 percent job approval once.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.869
He fell ass backward
into the job

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:40.439
the way your burnout cousin fell
ass backwards into that job

00:00:40.439 --> 00:00:43.309
dog sitting for a rich old lady
who was so senile

00:00:43.309 --> 00:00:45.445
she started thinking
he was her dead husband.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:47.347
So she put him in her will.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.549
And then, like after only a week
of working for her,

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.317
she died
and he inherited a fortune,

00:00:51.317 --> 00:00:53.018
and now he just
drives around town

00:00:53.018 --> 00:00:54.554
in the back
of a Rolls-Royce, screaming,

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.323
asking pedestrians
if they have any Gray Poupon.

00:00:57.323 --> 00:00:59.425
But one thing Trump was good at
was taking credit mostly

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.626
for things he had
nothing to do with.

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:02.929
He took credit
for a Veterans Choice program

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:05.198
that was signed
by President Obama in 2014,

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.232
not just once or twice.

00:01:07.232 --> 00:01:09.369
He did it over 150 times.

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:12.605
And at some point,
you just have to tip your hat

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:14.073
at his commitment to lying.

00:01:14.073 --> 00:01:16.509
I've never been that committed
to anything in my life.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.378
I don't think I even did
150 shows at "SNL."

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:22.148
I mean, I was there for well
over 150 shows,

00:01:22.148 --> 00:01:23.649
but it wasn't in all of them.

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:25.951
For some reason, they just
stopped using my John Kerry,

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:27.253
even though it's obviously

00:01:27.253 --> 00:01:29.422
still relevant today
now that he's climate czar.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:30.990
I've been emailing
Lauren suggesting that people

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.925
might want to see it again,
but it keeps getting

00:01:32.925 --> 00:01:34.327
bounced back
with what I'm guessing

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:36.729
is an auto generated reply
that says,

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.499
"Why won't you take no
for an answer?"

00:01:39.499 --> 00:01:41.267
Anyway, Trump took credit
for a lot of stuff,

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.970
so much so that when the first
round of Covid stimulus checks

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:47.840
went out last year, he insisted
that they put his name on them.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.575
That's a government check,
but it looks like

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.610
it came from Trump's
personal checking account,

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.579
which I doubt
has any money in it,

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:55.114
unless it was a secret
Chinese bank account.

00:01:55.114 --> 00:01:56.115
You guys remember that?

00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:57.050
That tiny little detail

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:58.617
that quickly got overlooked

00:01:58.617 --> 00:02:01.020
but would have otherwise been
a stunning bombshell twist

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.956
and an HBO prestige drama
starring Nicole Kidman

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:06.292
as a rich lady with a kid
at a fancy school.

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.127
My husband could never
have done this.

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:11.096
Ma'am, did you know about his
secret Chinese bank account?

00:02:11.096 --> 00:02:13.232
I need to go for a walk on
the beach to think about this.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.635
Give me my billowy shawl.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:18.071
Trump's one of those rich guys
who's technically a billionaire,

00:02:18.071 --> 00:02:19.906
but none of his money is liquid.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.407
To put a quarter
in a parking meter,

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:23.409
you'd have to sell
shares in Eric.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:27.280
Here's the new GameStop.
Father, no!

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.048
So Americans got a direct check
from Trump

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.783
with his name on it.
And you know what?

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:32.318
If that's how Republicans
are going to do things,

00:02:32.318 --> 00:02:34.220
the Democrats should
absolutely do the same thing.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.589
Send everyone a giant
game show check

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:38.725
that says, "From your best bud,
Joe Biden."

00:02:38.725 --> 00:02:40.993
For years centrist Democrats

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:43.562
have had a history of coming up
with well intentioned

00:02:43.562 --> 00:02:46.065
but super complicated,
hard to understand programs

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.902
instead of just giving
people things they need,

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.537
like money and health care.

00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:52.071
Instead of saying,
here's your check,

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:54.406
they say good news,
we passed tax credits

00:02:54.406 --> 00:02:56.842
for small businesses
that retrain coal miners

00:02:56.842 --> 00:02:58.510
to become pet therapists.

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.112
But then Democrats seem
to learn their lesson.

00:03:00.112 --> 00:03:03.716
They promised a lot of bold,
easy to understand programs

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:05.051
during the 2020 campaign

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.186
that would improve
lots of people's lives.

00:03:07.186 --> 00:03:09.355
And when Joe Biden
went to Georgia in January

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:10.990
for the Senate runoffs,

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:13.325
he made this very simple
promise.

00:03:13.325 --> 00:03:15.527
-By electing John
and the reverend,

00:03:15.527 --> 00:03:19.532
you can make an immediate
difference in your own lives,

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:22.968
the lives of the people
all across this country,

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:24.804
because their election

00:03:24.804 --> 00:03:27.740
will put an end
to the block in Washington

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.175
and that $2,000 stimulus check,

00:03:30.175 --> 00:03:33.045
that money that will go
out the door immediately.

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:34.680
-That's straight talking Joe.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.215
No bluster, no BS.

00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:38.685
He's the dad who says
if you get straight A's,

00:03:38.685 --> 00:03:40.152
he will take you to Dairy Queen.

00:03:40.152 --> 00:03:42.955
And when the ink is still hot
on the report card,

00:03:42.955 --> 00:03:44.657
your elbows deep
in your blizzard.

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:46.259
Finally, Democrats promise
something big

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:48.961
and straight forward
that will immediately materially

00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:50.362
improve people's lives.

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.398
By the way, not only did
that promise help win both

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.700
Senate seats in Georgia,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:56.602
the Democrats Covid bill
is incredibly popular.

00:03:56.602 --> 00:03:58.104
76 percent of Americans,

00:03:58.104 --> 00:04:00.406
including 60 percent
of Republicans, support it.

00:04:00.406 --> 00:04:01.707
76 percent.

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:04.343
You know how hard it is
to get 76 percent

00:04:04.343 --> 00:04:05.577
support for anything?

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:07.746
There isn't even
76 percent support

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:10.883
in my own family for my
Al Pacino impression.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.218
I mean, the kids love
Uncle Al,

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:15.655
[as Pacino] but wifey
is not on board.

00:04:18.123 --> 00:04:20.859
All Democrats have to do now
is have the fortitude

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:22.695
to stick together,
pass this thing

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:25.198
and get the money
into people's pockets ASAP.

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:28.167
So naturally, some moderate
Democrats are watering it down

00:04:28.167 --> 00:04:31.303
for absolutely no reason at all.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:34.374
-President Biden has conceded
to moderate Democrats

00:04:34.374 --> 00:04:36.342
agreeing to narrow income limits

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.544
for the next round
of stimulus checks.

00:04:38.544 --> 00:04:40.178
-Biden signing off
on an agreement

00:04:40.178 --> 00:04:41.513
to tighten eligibility

00:04:41.513 --> 00:04:43.549
for the stimulus checks
in the package,

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:47.152
now phasing out checks at
$80,000 for individuals,

00:04:47.152 --> 00:04:51.390
down from $100,000
and $160,000 for couples,

00:04:51.390 --> 00:04:53.492
down from $200,000.

00:04:53.492 --> 00:04:56.262
-Around 12 million fewer
adults and five million

00:04:56.262 --> 00:04:58.497
fewer kids
would get the stimulus payments

00:04:58.497 --> 00:05:00.432
under the new Biden Senate
compromise,

00:05:00.432 --> 00:05:03.636
according to
preliminary estimates.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.639
A lot of those adults are voters
who will now get less

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:09.275
in direct cash assistance
from President Biden

00:05:09.275 --> 00:05:11.143
than they did from Donald Trump.

00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:12.878
-Democrats,
what's wrong with you?

00:05:12.878 --> 00:05:15.314
Stop behaving like
your own opposition party.

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:16.849
Now is the time to go all in

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:20.486
while the GOP is distracted
by Potato Head's pronouns.

00:05:20.486 --> 00:05:22.521
Do you really want to risk
being seen

00:05:22.521 --> 00:05:24.523
as less generous
than Donald Trump,

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:27.393
the guy who infamously had
to shut down his charity

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:30.229
after he was accused of using it
as a personal checkbook to buy,

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:33.366
among other things, portraits of
himself and a football helmet

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:35.868
signed by Tim Tebow,
a guy who was so bad at football

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.471
he just retired
from a different sport.

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:40.139
What else did Trump buy
with the charity money?

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:43.075
A curling stone
signed by Johnny Manziel?

00:05:43.075 --> 00:05:44.777
Seriously, Democrats,
who's asking for this?

00:05:44.777 --> 00:05:46.379
Do you think there's
a group of people out there

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:48.047
who don't want a check.

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:49.816
Everyone wants a check.

00:05:49.816 --> 00:05:51.550
That's why there are
eight million game shows,

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.619
including one
where you can win money

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.221
just by hailing a cab.
And true story, guys.

00:05:56.221 --> 00:05:58.524
I hailed a cab last night
for the first time in a year.

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.693
It was the best.
Driver was blasting music.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:03.062
I was watching "Taxi TV,"
saw a "30 Rock" clip,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:04.530
emailed Tina Fey
to say how funny it was.

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.766
Windows down,
cold air blasted in.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.467
When we arrived,
it just strolled right out

00:06:08.467 --> 00:06:09.735
because in my head
it was an Uber.

00:06:09.735 --> 00:06:11.370
Driver started screaming,
"Hey, hey, hey."

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:13.639
I figured he finally
recognized me with my mask on.

00:06:13.639 --> 00:06:15.341
So I turn around,
I shoot him a thumbs up,

00:06:15.341 --> 00:06:17.110
only to see
that he is very angry.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.111
I apologetically get back
in the cab to pay

00:06:19.111 --> 00:06:21.147
and stay to watch the weather
on "Taxi TV."

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:22.749
New York is back, baby.

00:06:22.749 --> 00:06:24.884
I mean, it's not, but it's
getting closer and that's good.

00:06:24.884 --> 00:06:27.220
Anyway, the point is,
this is insane.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:28.621
It's political malpractice.

00:06:28.621 --> 00:06:30.056
The bill does lots
of good stuff.

00:06:30.056 --> 00:06:31.324
It's super popular

00:06:31.324 --> 00:06:33.125
and it gives money to people
who need and deserve it.

00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:35.862
Why would you make
fewer people eligible?

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:39.665
And by the way, taking checks
away from 17 million people

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:42.969
were reportedly only save
about $12 billion

00:06:42.969 --> 00:06:46.338
out of a $1.9 trillion bill.

00:06:46.338 --> 00:06:49.041
That's .6 percent.
Congrats, Moderates.

00:06:49.041 --> 00:06:51.744
You really proved
your fiscal bona fides.

00:06:51.744 --> 00:06:54.246
What's next? You can increase
the cost of a tasty cake

00:06:54.246 --> 00:06:56.048
from a vending machine
by 25 cents.

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:59.318
You really think anyone
you're taking a check away from

00:06:59.318 --> 00:07:01.187
is going to vote for you
because you're saving

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.788
$12 billion?

00:07:02.788 --> 00:07:04.156
Well, honey,
we won't get a check,

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:06.125
but at least they brought
the cost of the bill

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:07.893
down from $1.9 trillion

00:07:07.893 --> 00:07:10.662
to $1.888 trillion.

00:07:10.662 --> 00:07:12.265
What are the main drivers
of this push

00:07:12.265 --> 00:07:14.166
has been West Virginia Senator
Joe Manchin.

00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:16.502
Manchin has been
critical of the direct payments

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:17.937
from the beginning,
despite the fact

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:20.906
that they're all
overwhelmingly popular in polls

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:23.608
among voters
of every political stripe.

00:07:23.608 --> 00:07:26.245
In January, he told reporters,
"I don't ever remember

00:07:26.245 --> 00:07:29.548
FDR recommending sending
a damn penny to a human being.

00:07:29.548 --> 00:07:31.683
We gave 'em a job
and gave 'em a paycheck.

00:07:31.683 --> 00:07:34.053
Yeah. Jesus criminy,
can't we start

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:35.955
some infrastructure program

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:37.556
to help people, get 'em back
on their feet?

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:39.591
Do we have to keep
sending checks out?"

00:07:39.591 --> 00:07:41.661
Okay, first of all, why are you
talking like a character

00:07:41.661 --> 00:07:44.530
in a Frank Capra film?
Jesus criminy?

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.965
You trying to save the old
building and loan.

00:07:46.965 --> 00:07:49.234
Hey, Shoemaker.
Should I do my Jimmy Stewart?

00:07:49.234 --> 00:07:51.036
Okay, well...
Okay, you're waving your arms.

00:07:51.036 --> 00:07:53.005
It is very unclear
what you're trying to say.

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:55.240
Does this mean no?

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:56.608
Okay. Well, fine then.

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:58.344
Just stop moving around.

00:07:58.344 --> 00:08:00.012
You'll give me vertigo.

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:01.347
[Laughter]

00:08:05.417 --> 00:08:08.154
Also., do you remember
that FDR literally signed

00:08:08.154 --> 00:08:10.122
the Social Security bill
into law?

00:08:10.122 --> 00:08:11.223
Did you have a substitute

00:08:11.223 --> 00:08:13.225
for that entire year
in history class?

00:08:13.225 --> 00:08:14.726
Listen, I'm just
a field hockey coach,

00:08:14.726 --> 00:08:16.329
so all I know
is there was a civil war

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:17.730
and then Nixon was laughing.

00:08:17.730 --> 00:08:19.098
Now we're going to spend
the rest of the class

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:21.534
watching "Amadeus" on laserdisc.

00:08:21.534 --> 00:08:23.135
[ Blows ]

00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:24.970
Centrist Democrats
are also backing off

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.439
a $15 minimum wage,

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:29.508
which has the support of two
thirds of Americans in polls.

00:08:29.508 --> 00:08:32.444
The minimum wage hike was
originally included in the bill,

00:08:32.444 --> 00:08:34.747
but ruled ineligible
by the Senate parliamentarian

00:08:34.747 --> 00:08:36.515
for reasons
that are too stupid to explain.

00:08:36.515 --> 00:08:39.885
Basically, the gist is Democrats
have to use a process

00:08:39.885 --> 00:08:41.486
called budget reconciliation

00:08:41.486 --> 00:08:43.255
to pass the bill
with only 50 votes

00:08:43.255 --> 00:08:44.723
because the Joe Manchins
of the world

00:08:44.723 --> 00:08:46.992
won't just nuke the filibuster,
which they should.

00:08:46.992 --> 00:08:48.894
The reconciliation process
doesn't allow

00:08:48.894 --> 00:08:51.530
for so-called extraneous items,
and the person who gets to rule

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.699
What's extraneous
is the Senate parliamentarian,

00:08:53.699 --> 00:08:55.968
who advised
last week that the minimum wage

00:08:55.968 --> 00:08:57.536
was not allowed under the rules.

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:59.838
And hey, whatever you think
of the Senate parliamentarian,

00:08:59.838 --> 00:09:01.240
whoever they are,
they were elected

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.008
and elections
have consequences.

00:09:03.008 --> 00:09:04.242
What's that, Shoemaker.

00:09:04.242 --> 00:09:05.678
You're waving your hands again.

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:07.446
Was the Senate parliamentarian
not elected?

00:09:07.446 --> 00:09:09.649
Okay, it's just confusing
because you're using

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:11.384
the same waving motion
you used to tell me

00:09:11.384 --> 00:09:13.552
I shouldn't do
my Jimmy Stewart impression.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:17.757
Oh, help me out, Shoemaker,
you old so and so.

00:09:17.757 --> 00:09:21.994
Well, if it ain't Jimmy Stewart.

00:09:21.994 --> 00:09:23.896
Al Pacino?

00:09:23.896 --> 00:09:27.065
"The Man Who
Shot Liberty Valance"

00:09:27.065 --> 00:09:30.603
What serendipitous.

00:09:30.603 --> 00:09:33.372
Anyway, the parliamentarian is
in fact an unelected bureaucrats

00:09:33.372 --> 00:09:35.441
who basically just offer us
an advisory opinion.

00:09:35.441 --> 00:09:37.976
Republicans fired
the parliamentarian in 2001

00:09:37.976 --> 00:09:40.612
when they disagreed with
the parliamentarian's ruling,

00:09:40.612 --> 00:09:41.914
and no one cared.

00:09:41.914 --> 00:09:44.516
Democrats had the same power
to do the same thing now,

00:09:44.516 --> 00:09:47.787
or they could just ignore and
overrule the parliamentarian.

00:09:47.787 --> 00:09:49.622
That's what Senate Budget
Chairman

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:51.324
Bernie Sanders wants to do.

00:09:51.324 --> 00:09:54.060
-The idea that we have
a parliamentarian

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:58.497
who was elected by nobody,
who was simply a Senate staffer

00:09:58.497 --> 00:10:01.099
making a determination
that 30 million Americans

00:10:01.099 --> 00:10:03.869
are not going to get a pay raise
is to me unacceptable.

00:10:03.869 --> 00:10:06.305
So we're going to win this,
if not this week,

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:07.340
in the near future.

00:10:07.340 --> 00:10:08.707
-They'll be separate legislation

00:10:08.707 --> 00:10:10.643
if it's not included
in this legislation.

00:10:10.643 --> 00:10:11.877
Is that what you're saying?

00:10:11.877 --> 00:10:13.479
-I am saying that we are not
going to give up.

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:15.581
This is not going to be
the last vote on minimum wage.

00:10:15.581 --> 00:10:16.649
Trust me on that.

00:10:16.649 --> 00:10:18.417
We're sticking
with 15 bucks an hour,

00:10:18.417 --> 00:10:19.585
and I believe
we're going to pass that.

00:10:19.585 --> 00:10:22.554
-Yeah, people can't make
a living at $7.25

00:10:22.554 --> 00:10:24.223
-You're right.
-They are in poverty

00:10:24.223 --> 00:10:27.526
if they're working 40 hours
and only making $7.25.

00:10:27.526 --> 00:10:29.228
That's way, way too low,

00:10:29.228 --> 00:10:32.631
and it's been like that,
as we point out, since 2009.

00:10:32.631 --> 00:10:35.167
-Wow, the minimum wage hike
is so popular

00:10:35.167 --> 00:10:36.701
even Wolf Blitzer is on board.

00:10:36.701 --> 00:10:39.805
Wolf Blitzer, the man never
reveals what he thinks.

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:41.306
His wedding vows
where it will be

00:10:41.306 --> 00:10:45.143
very interesting to see
what happens going forward.

00:10:45.143 --> 00:10:46.712
He's an enigma.

00:10:46.712 --> 00:10:48.714
He doesn't even
make facial expressions.

00:10:48.714 --> 00:10:53.252
The Wolf Blitzer emoji is just
a circle with nothing in it.

00:10:53.252 --> 00:10:55.320
And it's true,
it is cruel and absurd,

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:57.089
to one,
tell people they can live

00:10:57.089 --> 00:10:59.458
in 2021 on $7.25 hour,
and two,

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:02.128
let an unelected bureaucrat
no one's ever heard of decide

00:11:02.128 --> 00:11:03.829
whether millions of Americans
get a raise.

00:11:03.829 --> 00:11:05.130
And by the way, do you know

00:11:05.130 --> 00:11:06.765
how hard it must be
for Bernie Sanders

00:11:06.765 --> 00:11:08.934
to ignore someone
whose title is parliamentarian?

00:11:08.934 --> 00:11:10.402
Bernie is the guy
who gets annoyed

00:11:10.402 --> 00:11:12.338
when other people
don't follow the rules.

00:11:12.338 --> 00:11:14.139
I bet he tells people
at the co-op to stop

00:11:14.139 --> 00:11:15.440
squeezing the melons.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.342
You get one squeeze
and that's it.

00:11:17.342 --> 00:11:19.211
They all came in
on the same truck.

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:22.415
Just pick a melon
and be done with it.

00:11:22.415 --> 00:11:25.184
We have a lot of people
here for melons.

00:11:25.184 --> 00:11:27.153
And the current parliamentarian
has reportedly issued

00:11:27.153 --> 00:11:28.853
other controversial rulings

00:11:28.853 --> 00:11:31.056
and what can be passed
under special budgetary rules.

00:11:31.056 --> 00:11:32.458
She ruled in 2017

00:11:32.458 --> 00:11:34.126
that Republicans
could add provisions

00:11:34.126 --> 00:11:35.994
to the Tax Cut and Jobs Act

00:11:35.994 --> 00:11:38.364
to open the Arctic National
Wildlife Refuge

00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:39.899
to Alaska oil drilling.

00:11:39.899 --> 00:11:41.667
Why is oil drilling
in the Arctic allowed

00:11:41.667 --> 00:11:43.068
but not a minimum wage hike?

00:11:43.068 --> 00:11:45.103
Trying to make heads
or tails of archaic Senate rules

00:11:45.103 --> 00:11:47.806
is like trying to
put together a shelf from IKEA.

00:11:47.806 --> 00:11:49.642
I don't understand.
It's just an outline of a man

00:11:49.642 --> 00:11:50.909
with an arrow pointing down

00:11:50.909 --> 00:11:52.778
and a question mark
next to his head.

00:11:52.778 --> 00:11:55.181
Above it,
it says klipphangare.

00:11:55.181 --> 00:11:56.415
Wait, that's not a klipphangare.

00:11:56.415 --> 00:11:59.884
This is a klipphangare.

00:11:59.884 --> 00:12:01.453
Sorry, people on YouTube.

00:12:01.453 --> 00:12:03.155
Sometimes we call back things

00:12:03.155 --> 00:12:06.991
that aren't in the body
of "A Closer Look."

00:12:06.991 --> 00:12:08.828
This is a whole show.

00:12:11.763 --> 00:12:14.066
But don't tell me
how to say bubar.

00:12:14.066 --> 00:12:15.401
[ Laughter ]

00:12:20.439 --> 00:12:22.741
Democrats need to pull out
all the stops to pass this thing

00:12:22.741 --> 00:12:24.310
because Republicans
are already making clear

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:26.045
they're going to pull out
all the stops to block it.

00:12:26.045 --> 00:12:27.979
Wisconsin Senator Ron Johnson,
for example,

00:12:27.979 --> 00:12:30.015
announced that he'd forced
the Senate clerks

00:12:30.015 --> 00:12:32.117
to read the entire bill
aloud on the floor,

00:12:32.117 --> 00:12:34.285
a formality which is
usually bypassed

00:12:34.285 --> 00:12:35.787
as a stonewalling tactic.

00:12:35.787 --> 00:12:36.955
-The first way
I'm going to resist

00:12:36.955 --> 00:12:39.792
is I'm going to go down
and object

00:12:39.792 --> 00:12:41.893
to the waiving
of the reading of the bill.

00:12:41.893 --> 00:12:45.764
I will make them read their
600 to 700 page bill.

00:12:45.764 --> 00:12:47.866
I'm going to lead the effort
to resistance

00:12:47.866 --> 00:12:50.068
starting today, I think,

00:12:50.068 --> 00:12:51.503
when they introduce
a substitute amendment.

00:12:51.503 --> 00:12:53.205
I'm going to make them
read that thing.

00:12:53.205 --> 00:12:54.573
Probably take about 10 hours.

00:12:54.573 --> 00:12:56.174
-You really think that's going
to be a deterrent?

00:12:56.174 --> 00:12:58.010
We've all been in quarantine
for a year.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:59.745
I've done things that are
a lot less exciting

00:12:59.745 --> 00:13:02.214
than listening to a bill
get read aloud for 10 hours.

00:13:02.214 --> 00:13:05.050
One time I just laid down on
the floor with a bottle of gin

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:06.585
and tried to guess
how many layers of paint

00:13:06.585 --> 00:13:07.953
there were on the ceiling.

00:13:07.953 --> 00:13:10.589
Turns out the ceiling's wood.
I was just super drunk.

00:13:10.589 --> 00:13:12.657
And my kids left me there.

00:13:12.657 --> 00:13:15.293
Seriously, people desperately
need help immediately,

00:13:15.293 --> 00:13:16.862
and you're playing
dumb procedural games

00:13:16.862 --> 00:13:18.330
to stop them from getting it.

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:19.364
And just to give you an idea

00:13:19.364 --> 00:13:21.200
of how dumb
Johnson's objections are,

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:23.068
yesterday he took the floor
of the Senate

00:13:23.068 --> 00:13:24.669
with a ludicrous poster

00:13:24.669 --> 00:13:26.906
to complain about
how much money was in the bill.

00:13:26.906 --> 00:13:30.409
-If you stacked million dollar
bills on top of each other,

00:13:30.409 --> 00:13:32.344
there would be -- they would
stack up to be

00:13:32.344 --> 00:13:34.679
358 feet high.

00:13:34.679 --> 00:13:40.552
So, how big would a stack
of a billion dollar bills be?

00:13:40.552 --> 00:13:43.689
It'd be 67.86 miles.

00:13:43.689 --> 00:13:47.259
So a stack of a billion dollars
would actually exceed

00:13:47.259 --> 00:13:50.328
the atmosphere
and extend into outer space.

00:13:50.328 --> 00:13:54.866
Well, how big would a stack
be of trillion dollar bills?

00:13:54.866 --> 00:13:56.535
Well, it's a thousand times
that,

00:13:56.535 --> 00:14:02.340
so it'd be 670,866 miles high.

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:05.644
We're talking about
$1.9 trillion,

00:14:05.644 --> 00:14:12.584
which would stack up
to 135,732 miles high.

00:14:12.584 --> 00:14:15.053
Madam President,
the distance to the moon

00:14:15.053 --> 00:14:19.624
is 238,900 miles.

00:14:19.624 --> 00:14:25.163
So that stack of $1.9 trillion
worth of one dollar bills

00:14:25.163 --> 00:14:27.533
would be more than halfway
to the moon.

00:14:27.533 --> 00:14:30.102
-Okay, Senator Snapple cap.

00:14:30.102 --> 00:14:34.072
Save it for your sci-fi movie,
"Money Stairs to Moon Town."

00:14:34.072 --> 00:14:35.707
Seriously, who cares?

00:14:35.707 --> 00:14:37.910
Also, where did you get
that dumb poster made?

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:40.379
Did you actually force a staffer
to go to Kinko's?

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:43.315
So, what's this for?
A sixth grade math project?

00:14:43.315 --> 00:14:45.183
No, it's for a congressman.

00:14:45.183 --> 00:14:47.218
There's a sixth-grader
in Congress?

00:14:47.218 --> 00:14:49.287
No,
He's an adult.

00:14:49.287 --> 00:14:51.790
Oh. Is it Ron Johnson?

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.058
Yeah.

00:14:53.058 --> 00:14:55.361
Democrats have lots
of bold agenda items

00:14:55.361 --> 00:14:56.996
that could immediately help
lots of people

00:14:56.996 --> 00:14:58.696
and fix
our broken political system,

00:14:58.696 --> 00:15:01.834
from the urgent voting reforms
in the For the People Act

00:15:01.834 --> 00:15:04.369
the House passed yesterday
to the Covid relief bill,

00:15:04.369 --> 00:15:06.138
but they need
to stiffen their spines,

00:15:06.138 --> 00:15:09.074
stop watering things down and
steamroll GOP obstructionists

00:15:09.074 --> 00:15:11.109
because Republicans
are so crazy, they're...

00:15:11.109 --> 00:15:13.411
-More than halfway to the moon.

00:15:13.411 --> 00:15:15.080
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:15:18.884 --> 00:15:19.985
God's Love We Deliver cooks

00:15:19.985 --> 00:15:21.653
and brings over
two million meals a year

00:15:21.653 --> 00:15:24.089
to men, women and children
living with HIV, AIDS,

00:15:24.089 --> 00:15:25.657
cancer
and other serious illnesses,

00:15:25.657 --> 00:15:27.158
and they need your help
now more than ever.

00:15:27.158 --> 00:15:30.161
If you're watching this online,
you can hit the donate button.

00:15:30.161 --> 00:15:32.898
Stay safe, wear a mask,
get vaccinated. We love you.

